.TH SDXI_UTIL 3
.SH NAME
sdxi_util \- generic libsdxi utility helpers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <sdxi/util.h>

const char *sdxi_err_str(int err);
const char *sdxi_err_name(int err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sdxi_err_name ()
returns a short stable token for a return code, such as
.B EINVAL
or
.BR ENOSPC .
.PP
.BR sdxi_err_str ()
returns a human-readable string for a return code. The string is stored in a
thread-local buffer and is overwritten by the next
.BR sdxi_err_str ()
call in the same thread.
.PP
Both helpers accept either positive errno values or libsdxi's negative
errno-style return values.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDXI (7),
.BR sdxi_types (3)
